# Design taste (binding)

Before changing code in this repository, read `docs/design-taste-and-preferences.md` in full and follow it.

- Frontend work: follow §2 (visual aesthetic, "Atelier Editorial") and §3 (UX principles). Reuse existing tokens, fonts and components; no new colors, shadows, boxed card grids or pills.
- Engine, service and backend work: follow §4 (architecture house style). `@dsa/intelligence` engines stay pure and I/O-free; wiring goes in `context.ts`.
- Hot paths (warm-up, review, re-solve, Today) stay zero-LLM and zero-network.
- If a request conflicts with the design doc, follow the doc and say so.

See also `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md`.
